{"band":1,"locale":"en","words":[["to do","I study.","To do — and the engine of Korean vocabulary. Attach it to a noun and you have a verb: 공부 study becomes 공부하다 to study, 사랑 love becomes 사랑하다. Hundreds of verbs are built this way."],["a car","I take the car.","A car. The same syllable is also the word for tea, so 차를 마셔요 is I drink tea and 차를 타요 is I get in a car. The verb tells you which one it is."],["woman","That woman is a doctor.",null],["I, me","I'm learning Korean.",null],["money","There is money in the wallet.",null],["the Sun","The sun is bright.",null],["we, us","We are friends.",null],["home, house","I'm going home.",null],["yes","Yes, that's right.","Three common words are spelled 네. This one is \"yes\". The others are \"your\" (네 책, your book) and the native number four before a counter (네 개, four things). Context separates them; nothing in the spelling does."],["to be in a place","I'm at home.","Korean uses one word where English uses two: 있다 is both to be somewhere and to have. 책상에 책이 있어요 is the book is on the desk; 시간이 있어요 is I have time. Its opposite is 없다."],["a hand","I write by hand.",null],["time","I don't have time.","Time in general, and also the counter for hours: 두 시간 is two hours. Do not confuse it with 시, which is the o'clock hour — 두 시 is two o'clock, a different thing entirely."],["I, me in polite speech","I am a student.",null],["dog","The dog is running.",null],["a bird","A bird is flying.",null],["door","I open the door.",null],["to go","I go to school.",null],["a body","I wash my body every day.",null],["room","The room is clean.",null],["eye","Your eyes are pretty.","The eye. Spelled identically to the word for snow, and in careful speech the two are told apart by length: the snow 눈 is drawn out, the eye 눈 is short. Most speakers rely on context instead."],["clothes","The clothes are pretty.",null],["you, informally","Where are you?",null],["head","My head hurts.",null],["to not have","I don't have money.",null],["a mouth","The mouth is small.",null],["water","I drink water.",null],["rain","It's raining.",null],["leg","My leg hurts.","A leg — yours, a table's, a chair's. The same word also means a bridge, which is why 다리를 건너요 is I cross a bridge and not something anatomical."],["face","I wash my face.",null],["why","Why are you late?",null],["school","The school is big.",null],["an arm","Your arms are long.",null],["human being, person","They are a good person.",null],["here","Please sit here.",null],["song","I sing a song.",null],["book","I read a book.",null],["the moon","The moon is bright.",null],["telephone, phone","I answer the phone.",null],["tree","The tree is tall.",null],["again","Please say it again.",null],["a day, 24 hours","The day is long.",null],["day","It's a good day.",null],["now, the current time","I'm going now.",null],["the world","The world is wide.",null],["a foot, feet","My feet are cold.",null],["to be late","The bus was late.",null],["entirety","Everyone has gathered.",null],["photograph, picture","I take a photo.",null],["a nose","My nose is blocked.",null],["bed","The bed is comfortable.",null],["mountain","I go to the mountain.",null],["hospital","I go to the hospital.",null],["one","One apple, please.",null],["gift","I like the gift.",null],["bag","The bag is heavy.",null],["music","The music is nice.",null],["today","The weather is nice today.",null],["to see","I watch a movie.",null],["really, truly","Thank you very much.","Really, truly — an intensifier before an adjective, as in 정말 좋아요. On its own, with a rise at the end, 정말? is the one-word question really?, which is how you will hear it most."],["store, shop","The shop is closed.",null],["the afternoon","Let's meet in the afternoon.",null],["road, path","The road is wide.",null],["coffee, especially the beverage","I drink coffee.",null],["rice, a meal","I eat rice.",null],["an ear","My ear hurts.",null],["picture","I draw a picture.",null],["bus","The bus is coming.",null],["a time","Please do it one more time.",null],["mum, mummy","Mum is cooking.",null],["alcohol","I don't drink alcohol.",null],["movie, film","The movie is fun.",null],["to buy, to purchase","I buy bread.",null],["the outside","It is raining outside.",null],["a star","The stars are shining.",null],["a plane","I take the plane.",null],["sky","The sky is blue.",null],["dad, papa","Good night, Dad.",null],["to come","My friend is coming.",null],["sea, ocean","The sea is wide.",null],["friend","I meet a friend.",null],["apple","The apple is sweet.",null],["a thing, an item","I buy things.",null],["hat, cap","I put on a hat.",null],["meat","I grill meat.",null],["something which is real or true","Is this real?",null],["shoes","I put on my shoes.",null],["a moment","Please wait just a moment.",null],["a birthday","Happy birthday.",null],["food, including drink","Korean food is delicious.",null],["five","Five people came.",null],["man","That man is my friend.",null],["two","There are two chairs.",null],["market","I buy vegetables at the market.",null],["opportunity","It's a good opportunity.",null],["cat","The cat is sleeping.",null],["window","Please close the window.",null],["summer","I go to the sea in summer.",null],["animal","I like animals.",null],["travel, a trip","I want to go travelling.",null],["night","There are many stars at night.","Night. Spelled the same as the word for a chestnut, which is a common autumn snack in Korea, so 밤을 먹어요 and 밤에 자요 are about very different things."],["to eat","I eat fruit.",null],["cow's milk","The milk is cold.",null],["bread","I eat bread.",null],["pants, trousers","The trousers are long.",null],["problem","There is a problem.",null],["clock, watch","I don't have a watch.",null],["a test, an exam","I have an exam tomorrow.",null],["to be good","I feel good.",null],["computer","I turn on the computer.",null],["city","The city is very big.",null],["the top","There is a hat on the bag.",null],["please, do go ahead","Welcome, please come in.",null],["dinner, the evening meal","I eat dinner.",null],["father","My father goes to work.",null],["the weather","The weather is good.",null],["paper","I draw a picture on paper.",null],["child, kid","The child is laughing.",null],["spring","Flowers bloom in spring.",null],["who","Who is that person?",null],["winter","It snows a lot in winter.",null],["when","When are you coming?",null],["lunch, luncheon","Let's have lunch together.",null],["where","Where is the toilet?",null],["hello and goodbye","Bye, see you again!",null],["over there","Over there is the school.",null],["a street","There are many people on the street.",null],["to know","I know the name.",null],["sometimes","I sometimes watch films.",null],["name","What is your name?",null],["the Earth","The Earth is round.",null],["sound","The sound is loud.",null],["a wall","I hang a picture on the wall.",null],["to live","I live in Seoul.",null],["chair, sofa","I sit on the chair.",null],["the world","I know many countries of the world.",null],["to ride, to get on","I take the bus.","To get on or into anything that carries you — a bus, a bike, a lift. Two other very common verbs share the spelling: 타다 also means to burn, and to stir something into a drink."],["thought","That's a good idea.",null],["park","I walk in the park.",null],["to be many","There are many people.",null],["to speak, to talk","Please speak slowly.",null],["son","My son goes to school.",null],["there","Is anyone there?",null],["family","I have a big family.",null],["the side","Please sit next to me.",null],["a village","The village is quiet.",null],["soup","I eat soup in the morning.",null],["morning","I get up in the morning.",null],["puppy","The puppy is small.",null],["a ball","I kick the ball.",null],["and, and then","I bought bread and milk.",null],["the first time","Nice to meet you for the first time.",null],["solitude","I can go alone.",null],["flower","The flower is pretty.",null],["map","I look at the map.",null],["autumn","The wind is cool in autumn.",null],["a daughter","My daughter goes to school.",null],["doctor","The doctor examines me.",null],["a colour","This colour is lovely.",null],["a little","Just a little, please.",null],["desk","There is a book on the desk.",null],["hello on the phone","Hello, who is this?",null],["tomorrow","See you tomorrow.",null],["very","It's very delicious.",null],["letter","I write a letter to my mother.",null],["too, excessively","These clothes are too big.",null],["a seat, a place","There are no seats.",null],["fruit","I like fruit.",null],["card","I'll pay by card.",null],["a cow","The cow eats grass.",null],["together with","Let's eat together.",null],["news, word from someone","I have good news.",null],["to give","I give a gift.",null],["no","No, I didn't go.",null],["a company, an office","I go to the office.",null],["that one","Please give me that.",null],["to be small","The shoes are small.",null],["a river","The river is very wide.",null],["the next, the following","See you next time.",null],["an egg","I eat an egg in the morning.",null],["to make a phone call","I'll call you later.",null],["Korea","I like Korean food.",null],["heart, mind","They have a warm heart.",null],["contact","Please contact me later.",null],["hotel","I slept at a hotel.",null],["kimchi","The kimchi is spicy.",null],["key","I don't have the key.",null],["a dragon","There is a big dragon in the picture.",null],["to read","I read the newspaper.",null],["the ground","The ground is wet.",null],["love","Love is beautiful.",null],["meal","Have you had your meal?",null],["to sleep","I go to bed early.",null],["a machine","The machine has broken down.",null],["automobile, car","The car is fast.",null],["an address","Please tell me the address.",null],["to be big","This bag is big.",null],["train","The train has left.",null],["to fly","A bird flies in the sky.",null],["a neck","My neck hurts.",null],["teacher","The teacher teaches.",null],["study","Studying is fun.",null],["early","I get up early tomorrow.",null],["mother","My mother is at home.",null],["but, however","It's raining. But I'll go.",null],["feeling, mood","How do you feel?",null],["the news","I watch the news.",null],["to be important","Health is the most important thing.",null],["building","That building is new.",null],["to want to","I want to go to Korea.",null],["readiness, preparation","Everything is ready.",null],["yesterday","It rained yesterday.",null],["to search, to look for","I'm looking for the key.",null],["quickly","Please come quickly.",null],["to be right, correct","This answer is right.",null],["to be visible, to be seen","I can see the mountain.",null],["sorry","Sorry, I'm late.",null],["a chat","Let's talk for a moment.",null],["she, her","She sings well.",null],["worry","I have a lot of worries.",null],["camera","I bought a camera.",null],["how","How do I get there?",null],["a shirt","I wear a white shirt.",null],["a neighbourhood","Our neighbourhood is quiet.",null],["this","Please give me this one.",null],["to throw away","Please throw it in the bin.",null],["words, what someone says","Please choose your words carefully.",null],["box","I open the box.",null],["the daytime","It is warm in the daytime.",null],["you, politely","I waited for you.",null],["to be pretty","The flowers are really pretty.",null],["restaurant","Where is the restaurant?",null],["how much, how many","How much is this?",null],["mirror","I look in the mirror.",null],["a miracle","That was truly like a miracle.",null],["to write","I write my name.","To write. The same verb also means to use something, to wear a hat or glasses on the head, and — as an adjective — to taste bitter. Four everyday meanings, one spelling."],["glass","The glass broke.",null],["a question","I have a question.",null],["just now","I arrived just now.",null],["below","The book is under the desk.",null],["still, not yet","They haven't come yet.",null],["to want","What do you want?",null],["grass","The grass is green.",null],["age of a person or other living thing","How old are you?",null],["to become","I want to become a doctor.","To become. It is also the everyday word for something working or being allowed: 안 돼요 means that will not do, and 다 됐어요 means it is finished. You will hear those far more often than the dictionary sense."],["an egg","The bird laid three eggs.",null],["to send, to dispatch","I send a letter.",null],["to put down, to place","I put the bag on the floor.",null],["a bank","The bank has opened.",null],["the floor","I wipe the floor.",null],["so, therefore","It's raining, so I'm not going.",null],["talk","It's an interesting story.",null],["bathroom","The toilet is clean.",null],["unweaned baby, child","The baby is sleeping.",null],["every day","I write Hangul every day.",null],["a week","Let's meet next week.",null],["station","Let's meet at the station.",null],["Seoul","Seoul is very big.",null],["stairs","There are many stairs.",null],["pig, swine","The pig is eating.",null],["a lot","Please eat a lot.",null],["already","It's already all over.",null],["other, different","Do you have other colours?",null],["continuation","It keeps raining.",null],["a fact","That is a fact.",null],["three","There are three apples.",null],["to be the same","Our bags are the same.",null],["to sit, to squat","I sat on the chair.",null],["a price","The price is high.",null],["taxi","Please call a taxi.",null],["student","There are many students in the classroom.",null],["a need","I don't need help.",null],["newspaper","Please read the newspaper.",null],["a reason","Please tell me the reason.",null],["younger sibling","My younger sibling is cute.","The one sibling word that does not change with the speaker: anyone younger is 동생, whoever is talking. Add a syllable when you need the sex — 남동생 for a younger brother, 여동생 for a younger sister."],["a chicken","The chicken lays an egg.",null],["treasure","The children are looking for treasure.",null],["an order","Would you like to order?",null],["ten","Please count to ten.","Here 열 is the native Korean ten, the one you use for counting things — 열 개, ten of them. A different 열 means a fever, and the verb 열다 means to open. Same two letters, three unrelated words."],["a cup","I pour water into the cup.",null],["to stand","I stand in line.",null],["the Korean language","Korean is interesting.",null],["rabbit","The rabbit hops.",null],["a price","The price is higher than expected.",null],["like this","Please write it like this.",null],["finger","My finger hurts.",null],["ice","Please add ice.",null],["nature","Nature is beautiful.",null],["driving","I'm learning to drive.",null],["information","I look for information.",null],["potato","I boil potatoes.",null],["cloud","There are many clouds.",null],["a medical patient","The patient is resting.",null],["a spring onion","I added a little spring onion to the soup.",null],["to think","I think so too.",null],["a kitchen","I cook in the kitchen.",null],["together","Let's go together.",null],["parents","Where are your parents?",null],["use","It's easy to use.",null],["all, every","Everyone laughed.",null],["airport","I arrived at the airport.",null],["to stamp","I stamped it with a seal.","To press something down onto a surface: a seal, a stamp, a fingerprint. The same verb covers taking a photograph — 사진을 찍다 — and dipping food into a sauce, all three from the one idea of pressing."],["grandmother","Grandmother is smiling.",null],["to not know, to be ignorant of","I don't know.",null],["swimming","I'm learning to swim.",null],["to not do","I don't drink coffee.",null],["country, nation","Korea is a beautiful country.",null],["the north","They went north.",null],["apartment building, block of flats","I live in an apartment.",null],["to work","My father works at a hospital.",null],["first in time or sequence","First I wash my hands.",null],["to join, to connect","I joined the two ropes.",null],["to receive","I received a gift.",null],["to sell","They sell fruit.",null],["one's parents","I live with my parents.",null],["to come out","Water is coming out.",null],["a beast","There was the sound of a beast in the forest.",null],["to go out","I'm going outside.",null],["most, the most","This one is the best.",null],["a forest","You can hear birdsong in the forest.",null],["an entrance","Let's meet at the entrance of the building.",null],["a dance","They danced on the stage.",null],["to grab, to catch","I hold your hand.",null],["to bloom","The flowers have bloomed.",null],["the capital city","The capital of Korea is Seoul.","The capital of a country. A separate 수도 means the mains water supply — 수도꼭지 is a tap, 수도 요금 is the water bill. The two are told apart entirely by what is around them."],["working out a total","The calculation is slightly wrong.",null],["the tongue","My tongue hurts, so I can't eat.",null],["help","I need help.",null],["homework","I finished my homework.",null],["a towel","I dry my hands with a towel.",null],["now, and now","Let's start now.",null],["what, what kind of","What work do you do?",null],["cooking","The cooking is delicious.",null],["a request, a favour","I have a favour to ask.",null],["a plate","Please take out two plates.",null],["to drink","I drink milk.",null],["salt","I add a little salt.",null],["an island","We took a boat to the island.",null],["to end","The class is over.",null],["especially","I especially like winter.",null],["to put, to place","I put the book on the desk.",null],["a quilt","The quilt is warm.",null],["no","No, I'm fine.",null],["the south","The south is warm.",null],["a greeting","I said hello.",null],["a moment, short time","Let's rest for a moment.",null],["to like","I like coffee.",null],["a start, a beginning","It's a good start.",null],["to draw, to paint","The child draws a tree.",null],["the won","It is two thousand won.",null],["the Internet","The Internet is slow.",null],["a bee","A bee landed on the flower.",null],["a vegetable","I eat a lot of vegetables.",null],["to pay","I'll pay today.",null],["a class","The class is interesting.",null],["year","I studied for two years.",null],["bicycle","I ride a bicycle.",null],["to touch","Please don't touch.",null],["sugar","I add a little sugar.",null],["a spacecraft","The spacecraft rose into the sky.",null],["dollar","It's a hundred dollars.",null],["a passport","Don't forget to bring the passport.",null],["a fly","A fly is buzzing around.","The insect. Korean writes the city Paris the same way, so 파리에 갔어요 means I went to Paris while 파리가 있어요 means there is a fly. Nothing but the sentence tells them apart."],["the best","This restaurant is the best.",null],["a classroom","The classroom is bright.",null],["a sweet, candy","I eat a sweet.",null],["probably","It will probably rain tomorrow.",null],["a young woman","A young woman is asking for directions.",null],["what kind of","What kind of colour do you like?",null],["an individual word","I learn a new word.",null],["everything, all","How much is it altogether?",null],["memory","I can't remember.",null],["an umbrella","It rained, so I bought an umbrella.",null],["to be tall","The building is tall.",null],["to meet","We meet often.",null],["to listen, to hear","I listen to music.",null],["to be unable to","I can't swim.",null],["the space between","There is a tree between the two houses.",null],["a mobile phone","I charge my mobile phone.",null],["to die","The flower in the pot died because it was not watered.",null],["wallet, purse","I lost my wallet.",null],["to be cute","The puppy is cute.",null],["still, even now","I am still waiting.",null],["a sock","The socks are warm.",null],["truck","A truck is passing by.",null],["to love","I love my family.",null],["a mobile phone","I lost my mobile phone.",null],["to be all right","I'm fine.",null],["wind","The wind is cool.",null],["police","Please call the police.",null],["a long time","I waited a long time.",null],["a fish","The fish is swimming.",null],["oil","I fry it in oil.",null],["to be cool, splendid","Your outfit looks great today.",null],["to wear, to put on","I put on clothes.",null],["handwriting","Your handwriting is lovely.",null],["elder brother of a female","My older brother is driving.","Korean picks the word for a sibling by the speaker's own gender: a woman calls her older brother 오빠, a man calls him 형. It is also used for an older man a woman is close to, which is why you hear it far outside families."],["older brother of a male","My older brother bought me a meal.","A man's word for an older brother. A woman would say 오빠 for the same person. Like 오빠, it extends to a close older man who is not family at all."],["weekend","I rest on the weekend.",null],["countryside, the country","The country air is good.",null],["hope","Please don't lose hope.",null],["glasses, spectacles","I wear glasses.",null],["thanks","Thanks for helping.",null],["a pencil","I draw a picture with a pencil.",null],["a road","The road is blocked.",null],["something, anything","What is this?",null],["to kill","I killed the mosquito that came into the room.",null],["the left side","Please turn to the left.",null],["a bowl","I put rice in the bowl.",null],["to open","I open the window.",null],["husband","My husband cooks.",null],["a moment, an instant","I can't forget that moment.",null],["freedom, liberty","Freedom is precious.",null],["to take time","It takes an hour.",null],["this time","I'll do it this time.",null],["a cigarette","The smell of cigarettes soaked into my clothes.",null],["once, one time","Please give it a try.",null],["football, soccer","I play football with my friend.",null],["to dig","I dig the ground.",null],["to begin","The class is beginning.",null],["life","Life is precious.",null],["gold","This ring is made of gold.",null],["a bone","The dog is holding a bone in its mouth.",null],["to be beautiful","The scenery is beautiful.",null],["a laboratory","I worked in the laboratory all day.",null],["a method, a way","There is a good way.",null],["a banana","I eat one banana in the morning.",null],["to dislike","I don't like cold days.",null],["knee","My knee hurts.",null],["a library","I borrowed a book from the library.",null],["wife, especially one's own","I came with my wife.",null],["thanks","I said thank you.",null],["a side dish","The side dishes are delicious.",null],["dried laver seaweed","We wrap rice in laver and eat it.",null],["the last one","I took the last bus.",null],["to be bad","The weather is bad.",null],["a year of age","I am twenty years old.",null],["one's hometown","I went to my hometown.",null],["cheese","I like cheese.",null],["popular song","I like Korean pop songs.",null],["to be short","The pencil is short.",null],["to use","May I use this room?",null],["the underground","I go by underground.",null],["grandfather","Grandfather reads the newspaper.",null],["to be so","Yes, that's so.",null],["secret","Please keep the secret.",null],["mistake","It's my fault.",null],["a facial expression","Their expression is bright.",null],["to do something well, to be good at","You sing well.",null],["good luck","Good luck with the exam.",null],["to make","I make bread.",null],["to wait for, to await","Please wait a moment.",null],["but, by the way","By the way, what is this?",null],["please","Please help me.",null],["an answer","I found the answer.",null],["never","Absolutely do not be late.",null],["this kind of","This is the first time for such a thing.",null],["university","I study at university.",null],["a promise, an appointment","I keep my promise.",null],["a plan","I made a plan.",null],["beer","The beer is cold.",null],["to put on shoes","I put on socks.",null],["practice","I practise every day.",null],["four","There are four chairs.",null],["to be cheap","This fruit is cheap.",null],["the right side","Please go to the right.",null],["peace","We wish for peace.",null],["to rest","Let's rest a little.",null],["a knife","I peeled the apple with a knife.",null],["appearance, figure","Their appearance has chang